# Invoice Emailer — credentials & environment
# ---------------------------------------------
# This workflow needs NO credentials and NO environment variables.
#
# All 16 nodes are Code / IF / Merge / Manual Trigger / Schedule Trigger /
# Sticky Note — workflow.json contains zero credential blocks, zero $env
# references and zero external API calls. This file exists only to complete
# the per-workflow folder contract; there is intentionally nothing to set
# below.
#
# Demo = the whole workflow, as shipped:
#   Import workflow.json → click "Test workflow". Done.
#   (The "Daily 9:00" schedule trigger is the production shape, not part of
#   the demo lane; it is inert until you activate the workflow.)
#
# Going live (optional, your own build — not part of this export):
#   - Replace "Intake: load invoices" with a real read emitting the same row
#     shape — a folder watch, an email-inbox trigger, or a Google Sheets node
#     (Google Sheets OAuth2 credential) pointed at your invoice sheet.
#   - Replace the inline `customers` map in "Lookup customer + dedup" with a
#     Sheets/Airtable read (same OAuth2/api-key credential), keeping the
#     { name, email } shape.
#   - Add a Gmail / Send Email node after "Compose invoice email" and map
#     to / subject / body / attachment (Gmail OAuth2 or SMTP credential).
#     The composed payload already matches those fields.
#   - Point "Alert owner" at Slack or email (Slack bot token / Gmail OAuth2).
#   Any such credentials live in n8n's credential store, not in this file.
#
# (intentionally empty — no values required)
